#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1609
#: includes/Admin/StatusReport.php:94
msgid "Shop type"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1619
msgid "Selects which price list is imported. The article list is the same for every shop type; only the selling price differs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1620
msgid "B2B also imports the retail price as a recommended retail price, stored on each product as _wksync_msrp. It is the figure a business can resell at, and it is left off any article Kontor lists no retail price for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1624
msgid "Connection test"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1627
msgid "Test connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1647
msgid "Shop"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1659
msgid "Fetch shops"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1668
msgid "Identifies this store in Kontor. The order, delivery and invoice jobs all need one, and so does the category import, because Kontor holds a separate category tree per shop. The stock sync does not use it at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1675
msgid "Products"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1678
msgid "Manufacturers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1705
msgid "Manufacturers to import"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1706
msgid "Every manufacturer is imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1716
msgid "Fetch manufacturers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1719
msgid "Import everything"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1740
msgid "Tick the manufacturers to import. Fetch the list to add more; leave every box clear to import the whole catalogue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1743
msgid "Narrowing this drafts products."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1744
msgid "Articles the filter excludes are no longer in the feed, so the next product sync drafts the ones it previously imported. Widening the filter again republishes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1751
msgid "Image base URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1761
msgid "Kontor returns image filenames rather than URLs. Set the folder they live in to import product images; leave blank to skip images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1765
msgid "Articles without images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1784
msgid "Only import articles that Kontor lists an image for"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1787
msgid "An article with no image is passed over rather than created. The check is on what Kontor sends, not on the shop, so a product whose pictures are still downloading is never caught by it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1790
msgid "This drafts products already imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1791
msgid "A product this plugin imported whose article now arrives without an image is drafted, exactly as one Kontor stopped listing is. It is republished by itself as soon as the article has an image again, or when this setting is turned off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1796
msgid "Sales quantities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1814
msgid "Hold customers to the quantities Kontor sells each article in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1817
msgid "Kontor states a smallest quantity and a step for every article, imported as _wksync_min_qty and _wksync_qty_step. An article sold in sixes with a step of two can then only be bought as 6, 8, 10 and so on — in the quantity box, in the cart and at checkout alike."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1820
msgid "Leave it clear to ignore them. The figures are still imported, so turning this on takes effect immediately rather than after the next product sync. Order screens and refunds are never restricted by it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1823
msgid "Both figures are shown on each product's Inventory tab, where they are read-only: Kontor supplies them and every sync rewrites them, so they are changed in the ERP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1828
msgid "Articles without stock records"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1846
msgid "Draft imported products the stock feed does not carry"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1849
msgid "Kontor's stock list is narrower than its catalogue: it holds no record at all for some articles the catalogue lists. Left clear, those products keep the level they last had and stay published, and whether Kontor still sells an article is left to the product sync to answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1852
msgid "Ticking this hides a large part of the catalogue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1853
msgid "On the account this was built against the catalogue lists 4386 articles and the stock feed carries 2945, so the first run after ticking it drafts some 1400 products. Each one comes back by itself as soon as a stock level for it arrives again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1856
msgid "Clearing it again republishes what it drafted, on the next stock sync — unless the product sync is holding the product back for its own reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1861
msgid "Products Kontor does not list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1881
msgid "Move products this plugin did not import to the trash"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1884
msgid "Leave it clear and a product this plugin never imported is left alone for ever, whoever made it and whatever its article number. Tick it only where the shop sells Kontor's catalogue and nothing besides."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1887
msgid "This removes products from the shop."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1888
msgid "At the end of each product sync, every product with no article number of Kontor's — and every product whose article number the catalogue did not carry in that run — is moved to the trash, whether it is published, private or a draft. Products made by another plugin, by an importer or by hand all count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1891
msgid "They go to the trash rather than being deleted, so Products → Trash is the way back and nothing is lost until the trash is emptied. Their images are kept in the media library either way, because a restored product needs them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1894
msgid "Clearing this setting again stops the sweeping, but it does not empty the trash and it does not restore anything already trashed. Restoring is done in Products → Trash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1897
msgid "A product whose article Kontor lists but is holding back — switched off for the webshop, or without an image — is never trashed by this. It was in the catalogue, which is the whole question being asked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1903
#: includes/Sync/Scheduler.php:202
msgid "Product sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1918
#: includes/Sync/Scheduler.php:210
msgid "Stock sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1933
msgid "Categories"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1936
msgid "Categories from Kontor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1947
msgid "Let Kontor decide which categories a product is in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1951
msgid "Categories will not be imported until a shop is chosen above. Kontor holds a separate category tree per shop, and asks for one before it will list any."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1955
msgid "The category tree Kontor holds for the chosen shop becomes WooCommerce product categories, matched on Kontor's own category ID so that renaming or moving one in the ERP is followed here rather than duplicated. Each product is then filed as its article says."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1958
msgid "Categories you added in WooCommerce are left on their products untouched, and so is any category Kontor has stopped listing. Nothing here ever deletes a category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1961
msgid "Turning this on or off rewrites the whole catalogue on the next run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1962
msgid "The category field joins the change check with it, so every article counts as changed once. That is the same cost as changing the shop type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1971
msgid "Articles with no category"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1982
msgid "Hold them back as drafts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1985
msgid "An article Kontor files under no category is imported as a draft rather than put on sale, the same answer this plugin gives an article with no image. It keeps its price, its stock and its pictures, and a category added in Kontor publishes it on the next run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1988
msgid "This is usually a large number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1989
msgid "On the account this was measured against, close to half the catalogue belonged to no category at all. Check the run summary before assuming something went wrong."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1996
msgid "Product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1998
msgid "Both rows are added to the product meta block, beside the article number and the categories, and each is shown only on a product that has the figure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2002
msgid "Recommended retail price"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2020
msgid "Show the recommended retail price on the product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2023
#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2056
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2034
msgid "Kontor supplies this figure on a wholesale shop only, where it sells at Ek and the UVP beside it is the price a business buying here can resell at. It is imported as _wksync_msrp and, until now, nothing rendered it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2037
msgid "The label is shown in front of the amount. Leave it empty for the default wording in the shop's language, and remember that it is what the customer reads: the figure is stated raw, not as a saving, and Kontor lists a retail price no higher than the shop's own for a small number of articles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2042
msgid "EAN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2053
msgid "Show the EAN on the product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2067
msgid "The EAN Kontor sends as Artean, held in WooCommerce's own GTIN field. EANs repeat across articles in the feed and WooCommerce refuses a duplicate, so a product whose EAN another already holds has none and shows no row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2073
msgid "Orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2076
msgid "Orders with Kontor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2094
msgid "Send orders to Kontor, and bring deliveries and invoices back"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2097
msgid "Leave this off for a shop that only imports the catalogue. Nothing is sent at checkout and the three jobs below never run. Turning it back on restores the schedules exactly as they were."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2115
msgid "Upload user ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2133
msgid "Sent with every order upload as meta.userId. Fixed by agreement with Kontor and not editable here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2138
msgid "Send orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2149
msgid "Sending as they are paid reaches Kontor within a minute of checkout. Either way the sweep below catches whatever that moment missed, so this is a choice about the ordinary path rather than about reliability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2153
msgid "Nothing will send orders on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2154
msgid "With the sweep below set to Never as well, an order reaches Kontor only when Run now is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2161
#: includes/Admin/StatusReport.php:105
#: includes/Sync/Scheduler.php:218
msgid "Order sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2172
msgid "A sweep for whatever the moment above missed — an order Kontor rejected, or one placed while the site could not reach it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2177
#: includes/Sync/Scheduler.php:227
msgid "Delivery sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2188
msgid "Pulls tracking details back from Kontor. An order Kontor reports as completed is completed here too, which emails the customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2193
#: includes/Sync/Scheduler.php:236
msgid "Invoice sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2204
msgid "Downloads invoice PDFs from Kontor. Each invoice is stored privately, shown to the customer on their order, and attached to the order emails sent after it arrives."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to the WooCommerce email settings screen.
#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2221
#, php-format
msgid "The delivery and invoice syncs can also email the customer when tracking details or an invoice arrive. Both are switched off until you turn them on under %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2225
msgid "WooCommerce → Settings → Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2235
msgid "Scheduled jobs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2269
msgid "Send categories to Kontor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2273
msgid "This replaces the entire category tree Kontor holds for this shop with the product categories in WooCommerce. It is not an import in reverse and it is not additive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2276
msgid "A category that is not in what gets sent is deleted in Kontor, and the product assignments on it go with it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2277
msgid "A category that came from Kontor is sent back under Kontor's own ID, which is what keeps its assignments attached. One created here is sent under a new ID and starts empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2280
msgid "Kontor's exact behaviour here has not been established against a live account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2281
msgid "Read the preview first. It shows exactly what would be sent and sends nothing. This runs in this request rather than in the background, so leave the page open until it answers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:2293
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

